				<h1 id="versionHeadLine" class="headline">

Elections		</h1>
	
		<div id="cc5f8c90dc-b4cb-431b-90ee-10648f8df655" data-containerid="5f8c90dc-b4cb-431b-90ee-10648f8df655" class="pageContent cpGrid cpGrid24"  data-contentcontainerbreakpoint="30" >
			

		<div class="row outer wide"><!--
--><div class="outer col col24 first last" style="" data-widgetcontainerid="1cb7bec7-328f-4b20-a828-9a5d72681f12">				
	<div class="row nest first last wide">
	
	<div class="inner col col24 first last id97598329-9a87-47e0-9718-91467e6cf6e6" style="" data-widgetcontainerid="97598329-9a87-47e0-9718-91467e6cf6e6">	
<div class="widget editor pageStyles narrow" id="divEditor6d81fba1-f913-4145-bc51-576efe51dfc2" data-elementqueryclasses='{"wide-narrow":"min-width:25em"}'>
	    <div class="fr-view">


        <h2 class="subhead1">City Elections</h2><p data-pasted="true">The City of Stonecrest operates under the direction of the Mayor and City Council. The Mayor and City Council consist of the following:</p><ul><li>Mayor</li><li>Councilmember, District 1</li><li>Councilmember, District 2</li><li>Councilmember, District 3</li><li>Councilmember, District 4</li><li>Councilmember, District 5</li></ul><p data-pasted="true">A Special Election for the City of Stonecrest will be held on <strong>November 3, 2026</strong>, for the purpose of electing one (1) City Council member.&nbsp;</p><p>The council member seat included in this election is District 2.</p><p>Qualifying will be held at Stonecrest City Hall, 3120 Stonecrest Boulevard, Suite 190, Stonecrest, GA 30038, August 10, 2026, thru August 14, 2026, as follows:</p><table style="width: 100%; margin: auto; border-width: 1px; border-style: solid; height: 188px;"><thead><tr style="height: 31px;"><th><strong>Day</strong></th><th><strong>Hours</strong></th></tr></thead><colgroup><col style="width: 50.0000%;"><col style="width: 50.0000%;"></colgroup><tbody><tr style="height: 31px;"><td>Monday, August 10th</td><td>8:30 am &ndash; 12 pm and 1 pm &ndash; 4:30 pm</td></tr><tr style="height: 31px;"><td>Tuesday, August 11th</td><td>8:30 am &ndash; 12 pm and 1 pm &ndash; 4:30 pm</td></tr><tr style="height: 31px;"><td>Wednesday, August 12th</td><td>8:30 am &ndash; 12 pm and 1 pm &ndash; 4:30 pm</td></tr><tr style="height: 31px;"><td>Thursday, August 13th</td><td>8:30 am &ndash; 12 pm and 1 pm &ndash; 4:30 pm</td></tr><tr><td style="vertical-align: top;">Friday, August 14th</td><td>8:30 am &ndash; 12 pm and 1 pm &ndash; 4:30 pm</td></tr></tbody></table><p><br></p><p>It is not a requirement to schedule an appointment for qualifying; however, if you would like to do so, please send your requested date and time to <a data-fr-linked="true" href="mailto:cityclerk@stonecrestga.gov" data-pasted="true">cityclerk@stonecrestga.gov</a>.&nbsp;</p><p><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/1931" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="docaccess-activated docaccess-status-disabled">2026 Qualifying Documents</a></p><p><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/1943" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="docaccess-activated docaccess-status-disabled">2026 Public Notice of Election</a></p><p><img src="/ImageRepository/Document?documentId=1961" class="fr-fil fr-dib" alt="2026 Elections Notice Aug 14" style="width: 419px;"></p><p>View a map of the <a href="https://experience.arcgis.com/experience/cd7e36c295ef445c94a9eaf889286c16/page/Council-Districts">City voting districts</a>.</p><h2 class="subhead1">Terms &amp; Qualifications</h2><p>Council members are elected to four-year terms. The mayor is also elected to a four-year term, but elected at-large. To be eligible to run for a city council seat, a person must:</p><ol><li>Be 21 years of age;</li><li>Have resided in the city and in the district the person seeks to represent for at least one year;</li><li>Be a qualified elector of the city;</li><li>Meet any other requirements as established by state law.</li></ol><p>The Mayor and Council serve staggered terms. The following are the terms currently being served:</p><ul><li>Mayor - 01/01/2024 to 12/31/2027</li><li>Councilmember, District 1 - 01/01/2022 to 12/31/2029</li><li>Councilmember, District 2 - 01/01/2024 to 12/31/2027</li><li>Councilmember, District 3 - 11/17/2022 to 12/31/2029</li><li>Councilmember, District 4 - 01/01/2024 to 12/31/2027</li><li>Councilmember, District 5 - 01/01/2022 to 12/31/2029</li></ul><h2 class="subhead1">Voter Information &amp; Helpful Resources</h2><ul><li id="isPasted"><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/1539" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="docaccess-activated docaccess-status-disabled">Election Day Polling Places</a></li><li id="isPasted">To find your district, please view our <a href="https://experience.arcgis.com/experience/cd7e36c295ef445c94a9eaf889286c16/page/Council-Districts">interactive map</a>.</li><li><a href="https://www.dekalbcountyga.gov/voter-registration-elections/absentee-information">Absentee Voting</a></li><li><a href="https://www.dekalbcountyga.gov/voter-registration-elections/early-voting">Early Voting</a></li><li><a href="https://www.dekalbcountyga.gov/voter-registration-elections/election-day">Election Day</a></li><li>Visit Georgia&apos;s <a href="https://mvp.sos.ga.gov/s/">My Voter Page</a> to find your polling location/precinct and additional voting information.</li><li>City of Stonecrest elections are managed by DeKalb County. For more details, visit the county&apos;s <a href="https://www.dekalbcountyga.gov/voter-registration-elections/our-mission">Voter Registration &amp; Elections</a> page.</li><li>To register to vote, or to check your voting status, visit Georgia&apos;s <a href="https://mvp.sos.ga.gov/s/voter-registration?IsRegisterNow=true#no-back-button">Online Voter Registration System</a>.</li></ul><p>To register to vote, you must:</p><ul><li>Be a citizen of the United States</li><li>Be a legal resident of Georgia</li><li>Be at least 17&frac12; years of age (and at least 18 to vote)</li><li>Not be serving a sentence for a conviction of a felony involving moral turpitude</li><li>Have not been found mentally incompetent by a judge</li></ul>
    </div>

